Interpretation
  B=14 refutes a global raw 2p1/5 tax: one row reaches 7071/17584.
  That row is shell-1 damaged, missing the tower bit 2.
  In this scan every shell-1-full row remains below 2p1/5.
  This supports the ordered target from HYP-2666:
    shell-1 damaged rows route to tower/mouth rigidity;
    shell-1-full rows keep the 2p1/5 p1-tax target.
  The full B=14 bank remains below 5p1/12 and keeps positive cap slack in this bank,
  but the sharper proof target is still shell-gated 2p1/5, not a looser global ceiling.

